    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 notes (dated 2026-10-20) to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, using the house format:\n\n```\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- None.\n\n### Features\n- You can now export reports as CSV from the report command. [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads now retry automatically with backoff when the server is temporarily unavailable (HTTP 503). [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- Fixed a crash when the config file is empty. [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Fixed incorrect totals in the monthly summary for leap years. [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\nACME-421 is left out, as you asked. It was the only breaking change in the list (removing the `--legacy` flag from sync), so that section now says \"None.\" If the revert means `--legacy` still works, that's correct. The older v2.3.0 and v2.2.0 entries are unchanged.",
